WHAT YOU MAY DO WITH THIS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Fork it, adapt it, run it commercially, ship products built on it. Apache-2.0
covers everything here: the service, the deterministic gates, the policy tables,
the workflows, the skills, the eval suite, the demo and recording tooling, the
site, the artifact chain, and `Agentic-SDLC-Playbook.md` itself.

The licence is deliberately permissive and deliberately Apache rather than MIT:
Apache-2.0 carries an express patent grant, which is what an enterprise legal
review asks about before anyone is allowed to adopt a reference implementation.

This matters more here than it would elsewhere. The repository's central argument
is that an operating model must be portable — that you can change your mind about
a vendor without rebuilding your controls. A portability claim is worth nothing if
the terms under which you may take the thing are ambiguous. So they are not.

The README's "Adopting this" section means what it says.

